  "scientific_review": [
    "The35previous projection objects and all old projectionCSVcells remain exactly preserved. Six new dated reference cases assess frozen North Brazil/North Atlantic/Labrador sources fromJanuary15/July15,2022. All44original source anchors and38neighboring intervals remain retained, with per-object primary10cm/s(North Brazil)/5cm/s(North Atlantic/Labrador) and original branch scopes.",
    "Three new cases contain supported regional descriptors and enter projections;three fully blocked cases enter unresolved_reference_cases instead. North Brazil has no eligible interior resolved node in either date:all14source selections are window-edge maxima or no-core cases. It has two discoverable unresolved caseIDs, no projectionIDs and an explicit reference_cases_blocked_no_supported_projection status. North Atlantic also retains one fully blocked date separately from its supported date.",
    "Supported ownership therefore rises from15to17current identities, with38supported scenarios total, rather than inflating it to18identities/41projections by counting completely unresolved cases. There are94identities without supported projection:one with only blocked reference cases and93without any regional reference case. This is support coverage, not current existence, physical completeness or whole-route depth coverage.",
    "All new cases retain the frozen neighboring-node model projection operator. Nine source nodes qualify for lower-depth projection and twoof38adjacent intervals support conditional interpolation;36intervals remain gaps. Original source vertices are never removed to connect a remote eligible pair. Exact blocked nodes and both neighboring intervals remain unknown; no extrapolation, threshold substitution or hidden alternate-node selection occurs.",
    "Projected primary lower depth remains distinct from paired model upper depth and layer span. Pair support is required before interpolating a model layer span, with thickness using a distance datum and physical_thickness_m remaining null. Native0m surface support, missing-level censoring and actual selected-node thresholds remain source properties, not bathymetry or whole-current bottom assumptions.",
    "The separate unresolvedCSV exports each blocked original anchor, exact raw model lower descriptor when present, source file/profile pointer, selected native/wrapped coordinate and explicit block reasons. Its projected_depth_descriptor_m is always blank, never a copied edge-selected raw depth or zero. Fully blocked cases are excluded from the main projectionCSV and supported coverage count, while remaining inspectable in JSON and the typed unresolved export.",
    "The reference corridors are undated editorial geometry, not contemporaneous model axes, observed current paths, full footprints or lengths. No independent current-axis or second-product surface-velocity validation is claimed. Source fixed tangent frames, snapshot times, scalar units and thresholds remain per case;two dates do not establish an annual envelope, climatology, monthly observed means or independent occupations.",
    "Ten cloud tests cover previous35-object/CSV preservation and all canonical ownership IDs;all six cases/44anchors/38original intervals;North Brazil no-inflation semantics;disjoint supported/blocked collections and coverage decomposition;exact source descriptors/frames/coordinates;date/threshold/physical separation;rejection of fabricated values in an all-blocked case;source-versus-projected unresolvedCSV fields;direct source pins;and unchanged2.5MBper-file caps. Six baseline checks passed at the same source commit.",
    "Existing frozen v13source-case construction and v12projection helpers are reused unchanged. The15source collection checks and220complete velocity profiles remain separately source-linked by exact hashes;no new field retrieval or numerical source operator is introduced here. All701canonical scoped references and102eddy-size references remain preserved.",
    "All geometry/interpolation/classification and tests ran in cloud on one idle CPU. Local work prepared small metadata/code, verified proof/source hashes and retained exact cloud outputs. No local numerical tests, model processing, native/WASM/browser/server/runtime or UI integration occurred.",
    "JSON2269656B,projectionCSV1862739B and unresolvedCSV10965B are retained byte-exact and published in separate batches under unchanged3MBaggregate/2.5MBper-file publication caps. Source definitions and prior files are frozen;the visible earlier Spray upper200m core-definition clarification remains preserved.",
    "The next North Brazil task is improved geographically justified axis/section support, not widening the old search until a result appears or converting failed brackets into current absence. More current coverage, defensible time-dependent thickness, compatible lateral geometry/areas, volumes, physical state passage and annual depth envelopes remain unfinished. No full programme completion is asserted."
